window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-eea2edbcef587cb2"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"chatgpt-work-cloud-security\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"chatgpt-work\">ChatGPT Work 云端安全</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整的文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后附加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取文档页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT Work 是您现有 ChatGPT 工作区的一部分，并遵循该工作区适用的隐私、安全和数据处理政策。对 Business、Enterprise 和 Edu 工作区而言，现有保护措施包括传输中和静态数据加密；默认情况下，OpenAI 不使用业务数据训练其模型。</p> <p>如需了解安全控制概况，请参阅 <a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/pdf/chatgpt-work-enterprise-security.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT Work 企业安全白皮书（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>Work Cloud 还引入了托管式任务执行，以及可以访问已连接系统或执行授权操作的可选工具。请检查组织所启用功能的权限、保留设置和可用审计记录。</p> <p>功能和控制取决于工作区套餐、推出进度、配置和已连接的集成。更广泛的执行模型请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-18ad336d66dd572e\">ChatGPT Work 概述</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"security-at-a-glance\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">安全要点速览</h2> <ul> <li>云端执行运行在 OpenAI 管理的基础设施上。使用 Work Cloud 本地电脑访问的任务，也可以通过已连接电脑使用经批准的本地工具。</li> <li>云端任务不会从该设备继承本地文件、桌面应用、浏览器会话或私有网络访问权。</li> <li>已连接应用使用已授权账户的权限；该账户可以是个人、共享或代理拥有的账户。</li> <li>工作区和功能特定控制管理 Work 访问、本地执行、云端浏览、已连接应用，以及代码或 shell 网络。</li> <li>Business、Enterprise 和 Edu 工作区数据在传输中和静态时均经过加密，且默认不用于训练 OpenAI 模型。</li> <li>保留时间和审计可见性取决于数据类别、存储位置、事件和适用的产品配置。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"where-cloud-tasks-run\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">云端任务的运行位置</h2> <p>启用 Work Cloud 本地电脑访问后创建的新任务，由 OpenAI 云端负责协调；各步骤可以在云端执行，也可以在已连接且获准的电脑上执行。此功能仅适用于启用同步后创建的任务。现有任务（包括项目中的任务）会保留原有模式：仅在本地运行，或仅在云端运行且无法访问本地文件。要使用此功能，请新建任务。</p> <p>如果新一轮对话开始时电脑不可用，符合条件且已启用 Work Cloud 本地电脑访问的现有任务可以继续在云端容器中运行。云端容器无法访问不可用电脑上的文件或工具，也不会强制执行适用于本地执行的企业要求。任务不能在某一轮执行途中从本地切换到云端。</p> <p>需要访问电脑本地文件或工具的步骤，要求电脑保持联网并处于连接状态。工作区权限、受支持的策略和用户现有访问权限仍然适用。</p> <p>用户设备位于组织自有、由 IT 管理的信任边界内，不属于 OpenAI 运营的系统。云端执行仍发生在 OpenAI 管理的环境中；同步任务也可以在符合权限要求的前提下，单独通过已连接电脑使用经批准的本地工具。</p> <p>Work Cloud 使用 Codex 任务执行框架。Work 和 Codex 共享核心执行与隔离机制，但可用工具、权限和管理控制并不完全相同。客户控制工作区访问、已批准的连接，以及有意提供给任务的信息；OpenAI 管理托管执行环境。</p> <p>Work Cloud 在共享的 OpenAI 管理基础设施上运行。在当前受支持的执行路径中，任务运行在由虚拟机支持的沙箱中，执行状态与工作区内已验证身份的账户用户关联。Work 可以跨任务复用环境，也可以在保留符合条件状态的同时替换环境。这并不意味着每个任务都会获得新容器，也不意味着每个客户都有专用物理主机。客户不提供、托管或管理 Work Cloud 容器。</p> <p><a id=\"what-a-cloud-task-can-access\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">云端任务可以访问什么</h2> <p>云端任务可以使用通过已授权路径提供的信息：</p> <ul> <li>用户输入对话的信息。</li> <li>有意上传、从 Library 附加，或通过项目提供的文件。</li> <li>通过已启用应用和已授权账户连接检索的内容。</li> <li>通过已启用云端浏览器或其他允许的 Web 功能访问的网站内容，但要受适用访问控制的约束。</li> </ul> <p>云端执行环境不会直接继承电脑上的文件、已安装应用、浏览器会话或企业网络访问权。启用了 Work Cloud 本地电脑访问的任务可以另外调用已连接电脑上的经批准本地工具；这些本地调用仍受该电脑及其访问系统的控制和权限约束。</p> <p>已授权的连接可以通过自身的访问路径，提供来自内部系统的信息。该连接不会赋予云端任务对员工设备或网络的不受限制访问权。</p> <p><a id=\"apps-plugins-and-connected-accounts\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">应用、插件和已连接账户</h2> <p>应用可以让 Work 访问另一系统中的信息或操作。插件可以将应用用作其底层工具之一。将插件设为可用，并不会自动启用底层应用、授权账户，或批准集成可执行的每项操作。</p> <p>直接或通过插件使用已连接应用的任务，只有在以下条件成立时才能继续：</p> <ul> <li>工作区启用该应用，以及需要它的任何插件。</li> <li>用户具有必需的工作区或角色访问权。</li> <li>连接使用已授权的个人、共享或代理拥有的账户。</li> <li>已连接账户、已批准作用域和可用应用操作设置，允许所请求的信息或操作。</li> </ul> <p>对于支持 <strong>Action control</strong>（操作控制）的应用，管理员可以允许只读操作、所有操作或自定义操作集。<strong>App permissions</strong>（应用权限）控制 ChatGPT 何时会要求确认以使用应用。根据应用和工作区，选项可以包括 <strong>Always ask</strong>（始终询问）、<strong>Any changes</strong>（任何更改）、<strong>Important actions</strong>（重要操作）和 <strong>Never ask</strong>（从不询问）。选择 <strong>Any changes</strong> 时，受支持的读取可无需提示继续，而更改则需要确认。</p> <p>当已配置的策略允许时，已授权写入可以无需提示而运行。这不会扩大应用允许的操作、工作区访问权或已连接账户的权限。ChatGPT 仍然可以阻止某些高风险操作。</p> <p>确认插件及每个底层应用在工作区中可用。将角色访问、已连接账户授权和操作权限视为各自独立的决策进行检查。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">插件控制</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"personal-and-shared-connections\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">个人和共享连接</h3> <p>个人连接使用已连接员工在源系统中的权限。共享或代理拥有的连接使用其已连接账户的权限。该账户可能访问请求者使用个人账户无法访问的信息，或执行请求者无法执行的操作。</p> <p>启用共享连接前，限制该账户的权限和作用域，选择可以使用它的人，并检查它可以执行的操作。请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001143-chatgpt-workspace-agents-for-enterprise-and-business\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">工作区代理的连接和权限（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>从已连接应用检索的内容不会自动保存为 Library 文件。如果之后将内容保存到对话、项目、Library 或已同步索引，该副本会遵循其保存位置的规则。</p> <p><a id=\"cloud-browser-and-network-access\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">云端浏览器和网络访问</h2> <p>云端浏览器、Web 搜索、已连接应用，以及代码或 shell 网络是彼此分开的功能。限制其中一项并不会自动禁用其他项。</p> <p><a id=\"cloud-browser\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">云端浏览器</h3> <p>云端浏览器是 Work 任务可用于与网站交互的托管工具。在 Web 浏览器或桌面应用中打开 ChatGPT 并不会启用云端浏览；云端任务可以在没有它的情况下运行。</p> <p>托管浏览器不会继承用户的本地浏览器配置文件、打开的标签页、现有登录、已保存密码、密码管理器或浏览历史。在受支持的情况下，用户可以通过安全托管登录流程单独登录。这不会授予对其本地浏览器会话的访问权。</p> <p>受支持的网站交互可以包括公开表单，也可以在网站任务中结合来自已授权应用的信息。在可用情况下，网站权限包括 <strong>Always ask</strong>（始终询问）、<strong>Auto approve</strong>（自动批准）和 <strong>Always allow</strong>（始终允许）。<strong>Auto approve</strong> 会应用自动风险检查；<strong>Always allow</strong> 会移除交互式网站访问审查。二者都不会授予新的应用权限，也不会批准网站上的每项操作。后果重大的操作仍可能需要单独确认。</p> <p>在 <strong>Admin Console（管理控制台）&gt; Permissions（权限）&gt; Workspace default（工作区默认设置）&gt; Workspace capabilities（工作区功能）&gt; Let agents use cloud computers（允许智能体使用云端计算机）</strong> 中配置 <strong>Use a browser（使用浏览器）</strong> 和 <strong>Allow network access（允许网络访问）</strong>。这两项权限独立于 Work Cloud 访问权限。浏览器访问与代码或 shell 的网络访问应分别检查；关闭其中一项不会自动关闭另一项。</p> <p>启用 Work Cloud 时，如果相关云端计算机功能尚未开启，系统可能会提示你开启它们。这些权限由 dots、Work Cloud 和团队自动化共用；不同产品可用的功能有所差异。请仅开启组织政策允许的功能。</p> <p>之后如需查看，请前往 <strong>Admin Console（管理控制台）&gt; Permissions（权限）&gt; Workspace default（工作区默认设置）&gt; Workspace capabilities（工作区功能）&gt; Let agents use cloud computers（允许智能体使用云端计算机）</strong>。本地电脑访问需要单独选择启用。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">在 Work 云端权限提示中启用“使用浏览器”“允许网络访问”和“允许使用计算机”的示例。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-cloud/cloud-computer-permissions.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>在 Work 云端权限提示中启用“使用浏览器”“允许网络访问”和“允许使用计算机”的示例。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-cloud/cloud-computer-permissions.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>Enterprise 工作区中的 Work 任务要使用云端浏览器，用户需要同时拥有 Work 访问权限和云端浏览器访问权限。请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001280-using-cloud-browser-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在 ChatGPT 中使用云端浏览器（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>还要在 <strong>Admin Console（管理控制台）&gt; Permissions（权限）&gt; Workspace default（工作区默认设置）&gt; Workspace capabilities（工作区功能）&gt; Let agents use cloud computers（允许智能体使用云端计算机）</strong> 中检查 <strong>Allow computer use（允许使用计算机）</strong>。此控制也适用于 ChatGPT Work。<strong>Use password manager（使用密码管理器）</strong> 是直接位于 <strong>Workspace capabilities（工作区功能）</strong> 下方的单独权限，不属于 <strong>Let agents use cloud computers（允许智能体使用云端计算机）</strong> 组。它控制本地应用内浏览器和云端浏览器对密码管理器的访问。</p> <p><a id=\"code-and-shell-networking\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"shell\">代码和 shell 网络</h3> <p>代码或 shell 执行的公共互联网访问遵循其自身的网络策略。公共互联网访问关闭时，ChatGPT Work 必需的网络目的地仍可通过受管目的地允许列表访问。</p> <p>允许列表管理网络目的地，而不是 shell 命令。禁用代码或 shell 执行的公共互联网访问，并不会自动禁用云端浏览器、Web 搜索或已连接应用。当前代码运行或 shell 命令结束、执行环境刷新后，网络设置更改才会应用。</p> <p>请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-668fd22585595004\">代码和 shell 沙箱</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"data-handling-and-retention\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">数据处理和保留</h2> <p>启用了 Work Cloud 本地电脑访问的对话，即使某个工具步骤在已连接电脑上运行，仍会通过云端协调。请将发送给协调服务的数据，与留在设备上的文件分开评估。推广前，请确认此工作流适用的存储、保留、驻留和审计覆盖范围。</p> <p>Work Cloud 本地电脑访问不提供严格的零数据保留。数据驻留和推理驻留仅覆盖符合条件的内容，以及受支持的工作负载、地区和配置。Enterprise Key Management（EKM）仅覆盖符合条件工作区中受支持的存储内容。Work 不支持阿联酋推理驻留。如果组织要求 ZDR，请勿启用此功能。</p> <p>Work Cloud 遵循适用的 ChatGPT 工作区隐私和安全保护。请参阅<a href=\"https://openai.com/enterprise-privacy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">企业隐私（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>与云端任务关联的信息不遵循单一、通用的保留时间表：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th><strong>数据类别</strong></th> <th><strong>保留和删除行为</strong></th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Work 对话</td> <td>遵循工作区的对话保留设置。已删除聊天通常会计划在 30 天内永久删除，但要受已发布的安全、法律和去识别化例外情况约束。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>托管执行状态和快照</td> <td>遵循与对话和文件分开的生命周期。执行状态的访问范围限定于账户用户，工作区对话保留设置会影响符合条件的已存储快照。结束任务或删除聊天不会立即清除每个相关工件。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>保存到 Library 的文件</td> <td>已上传或生成文件遵循适用的 Library 和工作区保留规则。删除对话不会删除已保存到 Library 的文件。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>项目文件</td> <td>在被移除或项目被删除前，一直与项目关联，但要受适用删除规则约束。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>已保存记忆（启用时）</td> <td>遵循单独的记忆控制。删除对话不一定会删除现有的已保存记忆。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>短暂上传</td> <td>如果不适用其他保留设置，Library 之外符合条件的 Enterprise 临时上传可在 48 小时后过期。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>已连接应用内容</td> <td>源系统记录遵循该系统的政策。保存到对话、项目、Library 或已同步索引的副本遵循其保存位置的规则。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>云端浏览器数据</td> <td>托管浏览器数据与本地浏览器数据分开。用户可以通过适用设置删除已保存的云端浏览器 cookie。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>合规记录</td> <td>合规日志平台记录可用 30 天。导出副本遵循接收系统的保留政策。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>删除对话、移除 Library 文件或已保存记忆、断开应用连接和清除托管浏览器数据，都是各自分开的操作。请检查相关存储位置，不要假定一个操作会移除所有副本。请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8983778-chat-and-file-retention-policies-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">聊天和文件保留政策（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>保留对话和执行上下文有助于 Work 恢复被中断的任务并参考先前工作。设置保留期限时，请将这种连续性与安全要求一并考虑。</p> <p>符合条件的 Enterprise 和 Edu 工作区可以对受支持的已存储内容使用 Enterprise Key Management（企业密钥管理）；在需要客户管理加密时，其中包括受支持的托管执行快照。覆盖范围因数据类别和部署而异。轮换密钥不会删除现有数据，也不会自动拒绝对较早加密内容的访问。撤销或禁用密钥访问是另一项操作，可能会中断受支持的工作流。二者都不会取代保留或删除政策。</p> <p>数据驻留和推理驻留仅适用于符合条件的内容和受支持的工作负载，且受组织协议、区域和配置的约束。已连接应用、外部提供者和某些处理或已同步索引可能遵循不同的位置规则。请验证对产品、集成和区域的支持。请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9903489-data-residency-and-inference-residency-for-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">数据驻留和推理驻留（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>OpenAI API <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">零数据保留</a> 是 API 特定控制，它并不定义 ChatGPT Work 的保留行为。</p> <p><a id=\"administrator-access-controls\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">管理员访问控制</h2> <p>在 Work Cloud 下启用 <strong>允许本地电脑访问（Allow local computer access）</strong>。这不要求启用 <strong>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中本地使用 Codex（Use Codex locally on the ChatGPT desktop app）</strong>。如果任何云策略启用了 <code>enforce_residency</code>，Work 和 dots 的 <strong>允许本地电脑访问</strong> 都会被禁用。此安全措施不会配置工作区数据驻留，也不会单独关闭 Work Cloud 或 dots。启用前，请在 <strong>Agent Security</strong> 中检查或创建 Global 云策略基线。</p> <p>使用 Policy API 管理 Global 设置；管理 Local 或 Codex Cloud 设置时，请使用 Agent Security 界面。迁移后现有 Global API 工作流仍可使用。请测试脚本和 Terraform 集成，并确认策略分配和优先级顺序没有改变。有关 Policy API、迁移和 Terraform 的指导，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad?anchor=what-carries-over\">哪些设置会沿用</a>。</p> <p>请按适用范围分别检查各项控制：</p> <ul> <li> <p><strong>企业要求。</strong> 对于启用了本地访问的 Work 和 dots，启用托管策略后，受支持的 Global 策略会通过共享云端协调器生效。适用的本地 <code>requirements.toml</code> 要求约束已连接电脑上的执行。Work 云端容器和 dots 云端电脑使用各自的执行配置和要求，而非其他执行器类型使用的托管环境配置包。本地执行限制不会自动应用到这些云端电脑。请分别检查云端功能权限，并单独测试本地和云端执行。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>本地执行。</strong> 已连接电脑上执行的步骤仍受受支持的设备控制约束。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>云端执行策略。</strong> Work Cloud 根据现有 Work Cloud 策略管理自己的执行环境。本地环境的托管执行策略不会转移到云端；桌面浏览器站点规则也不会自动成为云端浏览器限制。</p> </li> </ul> <p>审批和网页搜索等协调器控制项应保留在 Global 中。在适用时使用专用的“允许的审批策略”和“允许的网页搜索模式”控制项，其他受支持字段则通过 TOML 配置。字段列表和执行范围请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>。</p> <p>关闭 Work Cloud 本地电脑访问会中断当前正在运行的轮次。用户可以在现有云端对话中开始新一轮；新一轮会自动使用 Work Cloud，但无法访问本地文件。</p> <p>请检查适用于云端任务各个部分的控制：</p> <ul> <li><strong>Work Cloud 和 Work Local：</strong> 在提供独立控制的情况下，请在 <strong>Workspace settings</strong>（工作区设置）&gt; <strong>Permissions &amp; roles</strong>（权限和角色）中将云端 Work 和本地 Work 作为不同控制管理。在其他工作区中，本地 Work 可以与 Codex Local 共享控制。</li> <li><strong>应用和插件：</strong> 选择哪些集成可用，以及哪些用户或角色可以使用它们。</li> <li><strong>已连接账户操作：</strong> 检查账户权限、应用作用域和可用的操作或确认控制。</li> <li><strong>浏览器和网络：</strong> 分别评估云端浏览器访问和代码或 shell 公共网络访问。</li> </ul> <p>仅为已批准用户或组启用 <strong>Work Cloud</strong>。如果想要仅限云端的 Work、但不启用跨设备同步，且工作区提供独立权限，请为目标角色启用 Work Cloud 并禁用 Work Local。跨设备同步需要同时具备这两项权限。关闭任一权限并保存更改，也会关闭 Sync。在本地 Work 与 Codex 共用一项控制的工作区中，禁用本地执行前请先检查对两者的影响。这些控制不会阻止已授权用户主动将文件上传到云端任务。</p> <p>对于支持 <strong>Default</strong>（默认）、<strong>On</strong>（开启）和 <strong>Off</strong>（关闭）的角色权限，<strong>Default</strong> 会继承工作区设置；<strong>On</strong> 表示通过该角色授予访问权限；<strong>Off</strong> 表示该角色不授予访问权限。普通角色权限以叠加方式组合，因此另一个已分配角色仍可能授予访问权限。锁定模式（Lockdown Mode）和产品资格另行适用。部分 Work 和插件设置使用不同的两状态控制。请核实所有已分配角色的实际权限。请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11750701-rbac\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">基于角色的访问控制（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>在可用情况下，<strong>Work Cloud</strong> 权限会跨受支持的 Web、移动和桌面体验生效。它不会独立选择其中哪个界面可以运行云端任务。如果部署必须排除特定界面，请考虑使用设备管理或其他访问控制。</p> <p><a id=\"audit-and-compliance-visibility\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">审计和合规可见性</h2> <p>对于符合条件的 Enterprise 和 Edu 工作区，合规日志平台可以包含受支持的 Work 提示词和响应。已连接应用调用有单独的日志，可用的源系统审计记录因集成而异。受支持的合规端点可以提供对符合条件的 Library 文件的访问权。</p> <p>覆盖范围取决于事件及事件发生的系统。不要假定每条 shell 命令、浏览器交互、应用调用、文件操作或批准都会出现在客户可见的合规导出中。</p> <p>端点监控可以观察受管设备上的 ChatGPT 客户端或网络流量，但无法检查托管执行环境内的操作。请改用受支持的 Work、合规和已连接系统记录。</p> <p>检查当前的合规事件覆盖范围，同时参考工作区报告、已连接系统审计日志，以及接收导出记录的系统所采用的保留政策。请参阅 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9261474-compliance-api-for-chatgpt-enterprise-edu-and-chatgpt-for-teachers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI 合规平台（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"verify-cloud-access-and-controls\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">验证云端访问与控制措施</h2> <p>使用符合团队工作实际的任务测试云端访问。例如，安全团队可以将已批准的供应商安全通告与已授权资产清单进行比较，并在决定后续操作之前检查暴露评估草稿。如果云端浏览或已连接应用不可用，请直接提供安全通告和已批准的清单摘录。</p> <p>只启用任务所需的访问权限。检查已连接账户的权限、数据保留设置和可用审计记录，并告知用户哪些结果和操作需要人工复核。有关推出规划，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">管理员推出指南</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"chatgpt-work-cloud-security\">ChatGPT Work cloud security</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT Work is part of your existing ChatGPT workspace and follows its applicable privacy, security, and data-handling policies. For Business, Enterprise, and Edu workspaces, existing protections include encryption in transit and at rest, and OpenAI doesn't use business data to train its models by default.</p> <p>For an overview of the security controls, see the <a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/pdf/chatgpt-work-enterprise-security.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT Work enterprise security whitepaper (online)</a>.</p> <p>Work Cloud also introduces hosted task execution and optional tools that can access connected systems or take authorized actions. Review the permissions, retention settings, and available audit records for the capabilities your organization enables.</p> <p>Capabilities and controls depend on the workspace plan, rollout, configuration, and connected integration. For the broader execution model, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-18ad336d66dd572e\">ChatGPT Work Overview</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"security-at-a-glance\">Security at a glance</h2> <ul> <li> <p>Cloud execution runs on OpenAI-managed infrastructure. A task using Local computer access with Work Cloud can also use approved local tools through a connected computer.</p> </li> <li> <p>The cloud environment does not automatically inherit local files, applications, browser sessions, or private-network access.</p> </li> <li> <p>Connected apps use the permissions of the authorized account, which can be an individual, shared, or agent-owned account.</p> </li> <li> <p>Workspace and feature-specific controls govern Work access, local execution, cloud browsing, connected apps, and code or shell networking.</p> </li> <li> <p>Business, Enterprise, and Edu workspace data is encrypted in transit and at rest and is not used to train OpenAI models by default.</p> </li> <li> <p>Retention and audit visibility depend on the data category, storage location, event, and product configuration.</p> </li> </ul> <h2 id=\"where-cloud-tasks-run\">Where cloud tasks run</h2> <p>For new tasks created after you enable Local computer access with Work Cloud, OpenAI's cloud coordinates the task while individual steps can execute in the cloud or on an approved, connected computer. This feature applies only to tasks created after you enable sync. Existing tasks, including tasks in projects, keep their original mode: locally only, or in the cloud without access to local files. Start a new task to use this feature.</p> <p>If the computer is unavailable when a new turn starts, an existing eligible task using local computer access with Work Cloud can continue in a cloud container. The cloud container cannot access files or tools on the unavailable computer. It also does not enforce enterprise requirements from local execution. A task cannot switch from local execution to the cloud during a turn.</p> <p>A step that needs a computer's local files or tools requires that computer to be online and connected. Workspace permissions, supported policy, and the user's existing access continue to apply.</p> <p>The user's device sits within the organization's own IT-managed trust boundary, outside OpenAI-operated systems. Cloud execution remains in the OpenAI-managed environment. A synced task can separately use approved local tools through a connected computer, subject to its permissions.</p> <p>Work Cloud uses the Codex task-execution harness. Work and Codex share core execution and isolation mechanisms, but their available tools, permissions, and administrative controls aren't identical. The customer controls workspace access, approved connections, and information intentionally supplied to a task. OpenAI manages the hosted execution environment.</p> <p>Work Cloud runs on shared, OpenAI-managed infrastructure. In the current supported execution path, tasks run in VM-backed sandboxes, with execution state associated with the authenticated account user in the workspace. Work can reuse an environment across tasks or replace it while preserving eligible state. This doesn't mean every task receives a new container or that each customer has a dedicated physical host. Customers don't provide, host, or manage Work Cloud containers.</p> <h2 id=\"what-a-cloud-task-can-access\">What a cloud task can access</h2> <p>A cloud task can use information made available through an authorized path:</p> <ul> <li> <p>Information a person enters into a conversation.</p> </li> <li> <p>Files intentionally uploaded, attached from Library, or made available through a project.</p> </li> <li> <p>Content retrieved through an enabled app and an authorized account connection.</p> </li> <li> <p>Website content accessed through an enabled cloud browser or another permitted web capability, subject to applicable access controls.</p> </li> </ul> <p>The cloud execution environment does not directly inherit a computer's files, installed applications, browser session, or corporate-network access. A task using Local computer access with Work Cloud can separately call approved local tools on a connected computer. Those local calls remain subject to the controls and permissions of that computer and the systems it accesses.</p> <p>An authorized connection can make information from an internal system available through its own access path. That connection doesn't give the cloud task unrestricted access to the employee's device or network.</p> <h2 id=\"apps-plugins-and-connected-accounts\">Apps, plugins, and connected accounts</h2> <p>An app can give Work access to information or actions in another system. A plugin can use an app as one of its underlying tools. Making a plugin available doesn't automatically enable the underlying app, authorize an account, or approve every action the integration can perform.</p> <p>A task that uses a connected app, directly or through a plugin, can proceed only when:</p> <ul> <li>The workspace enables the app and any plugin that requires it.</li> <li>The person has the necessary workspace or role access.</li> <li>The connection uses an authorized individual, shared, or agent-owned account.</li> <li>The connected account, approved scopes, and available app action settings permit the requested information or operation.</li> </ul> <p>For apps that support <strong>Action control</strong>, administrators can allow read-only actions, all actions, or a custom set. <strong>App permissions</strong> control when ChatGPT asks for confirmation to work with an app. Depending on the app and workspace, options can include <strong>Always ask</strong>, <strong>Any changes</strong>, <strong>Important actions</strong>, and <strong>Never ask</strong>. With <strong>Any changes</strong>, supported reads can proceed without a prompt while changes require confirmation.</p> <p>An authorized write can run without a prompt when the configured policy allows it. This doesn't expand the app's allowed actions, workspace access, or the connected account's permissions. ChatGPT can still block some high-risk actions.</p> <p>Confirm the plugin and each underlying app are available in the workspace. Review role access, connected-account authorization, and action permissions as distinct decisions. See <a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">Plugin controls</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"personal-and-shared-connections\">Personal and shared connections</h3> <p>A personal connection uses the connected employee's permissions in the source system. A shared or agent-owned connection uses the permissions of its connected account instead. That account might access information or perform actions that the requesting person couldn't access with a personal account.</p> <p>Before enabling a shared connection, limit the account's permissions and scopes, choose who can use it, and review the actions it can perform. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001143-chatgpt-workspace-agents-for-enterprise-and-business\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Workspace Agent connections and permissions (online)</a>.</p> <p>Content retrieved from a connected app isn't automatically saved as a Library file. If the content is later saved to a conversation, project, Library, or synced index, that copy follows the rules for its saved location.</p> <h2 id=\"cloud-browser-and-network-access\">Cloud browser and network access</h2> <p>The cloud browser, web search, connected apps, and code or shell networking are separate capabilities. Restricting one doesn't automatically disable the others.</p> <h3 id=\"cloud-browser\">Cloud browser</h3> <p>The cloud browser is a hosted tool a Work task can use to interact with websites. Opening ChatGPT in a web browser or desktop app doesn't enable cloud browsing; a cloud task can run without it.</p> <p>The hosted browser doesn't inherit the user's local browser profile, open tabs, existing sign-ins, saved passwords, password manager, or browsing history. Where supported, users can sign in separately through a secure hosted sign-in flow. This doesn't grant access to their local browser session.</p> <p>Supported website interactions can include public forms and can combine information from an authorized app with a website task. Where available, website permissions include <strong>Always ask</strong>, <strong>Auto approve</strong>, and <strong>Always allow</strong>. <strong>Auto approve</strong> applies automated risk checks; <strong>Always allow</strong> removes the interactive website-access review. Neither grants new app permissions or approves every action on a website. Consequential actions can still require separate confirmation.</p> <p>Configure <strong>Use a browser</strong> and <strong>Allow network access</strong> under <strong>Admin Console</strong> &gt; <strong>Permissions</strong> &gt; <strong>Workspace default</strong> &gt; <strong>Workspace capabilities</strong> &gt; <strong>Let agents use cloud computers</strong>. These permissions are independent of Work Cloud access. Review browser access and code or shell network access separately. Disabling one does not automatically disable the other.</p> <p>When you enable Work Cloud, you may be prompted to enable the relevant cloud computer capabilities if they are not already enabled. These permissions are shared across dots, Work Cloud, and team automations; available functionality varies by product. Enable the capabilities your organization’s policies allow.</p> <p>To review them later, go to <strong>Admin Console</strong> &gt; <strong>Permissions</strong> &gt; <strong>Workspace default</strong> &gt; <strong>Workspace capabilities</strong> &gt; <strong>Let agents use cloud computers</strong>. Local computer access is a separate opt-in.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Do more with Work in the cloud permission prompt with Use a browser, Allow network access, and Allow computer use enabled. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-cloud/cloud-computer-permissions.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Do more with Work in the cloud permission prompt with Use a browser, Allow network access, and Allow computer use enabled. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/work-cloud/cloud-computer-permissions.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>For a Work task to use the cloud browser in an Enterprise workspace, the user needs both Work access and cloud browser access. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001280-using-cloud-browser-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Using cloud browser in ChatGPT (online)</a>.</p> <p>Also review <strong>Allow computer use</strong> under <strong>Admin Console</strong> &gt; <strong>Permissions</strong> &gt; <strong>Workspace default</strong> &gt; <strong>Workspace capabilities</strong> &gt; <strong>Let agents use cloud computers</strong>. This control also applies to ChatGPT Work. <strong>Use password manager</strong> is a separate permission directly under <strong>Workspace capabilities</strong>, outside the <strong>Let agents use cloud computers</strong> group. It governs password-manager access in the local in-app browser and cloud browser.</p> <h3 id=\"code-and-shell-networking\">Code and shell networking</h3> <p>Public internet access for code or shell execution follows its own network policy. When public internet access is off, network destinations required for ChatGPT Work can remain reachable through a managed destination allowlist.</p> <p>The allowlist governs network destinations, not shell commands. Disabling public internet access for code or shell execution doesn't, by itself, disable the cloud browser, web search, or connected apps. Changes to the network setting apply after the current code run or shell command finishes and the execution environment refreshes.</p> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-668fd22585595004\">Code and shell sandboxing</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"data-handling-and-retention\">Data handling and retention</h2> <p>A conversation using Local computer access with Work Cloud uses cloud coordination even when a tool runs on a connected computer. Review the data sent to the orchestrating service separately from files remaining on the device. Confirm the applicable storage, retention, residency, and audit coverage for the workflow before rollout.</p> <p>Local computer access with Work Cloud does not provide strict zero data retention. Data residency and inference residency cover only eligible content and supported workloads, regions, and configurations. Enterprise Key Management (EKM) covers supported stored content in eligible workspaces. Work is not supported with UAE inference residency. If your organization requires ZDR, do not enable this feature.</p> <p>Work Cloud follows the applicable ChatGPT workspace privacy and security protections. See <a href=\"https://openai.com/enterprise-privacy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Enterprise privacy (online)</a>.</p> <p>Information associated with a cloud task doesn't follow one universal retention schedule:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th><strong>Data category</strong></th> <th><strong>Retention and deletion behavior</strong></th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Work conversations</td> <td>Follow the workspace conversation-retention settings. Deleted chats are generally scheduled for permanent deletion within 30 days, subject to published security, legal, and de-identification exceptions.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Hosted execution state and snapshots</td> <td>Follow a separate lifecycle from conversations and files. Access to execution state is scoped to the account user, and the workspace conversation-retention setting informs eligible stored snapshots. Ending a task or deleting a chat doesn't immediately purge every related artifact.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Files saved to Library</td> <td>Uploaded or generated files follow applicable Library and workspace retention rules. Deleting a conversation doesn't delete a file saved to Library.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Project files</td> <td>Remain associated with their project until removed or the project is deleted, subject to applicable deletion rules.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Saved memories, when enabled</td> <td>Follow separate memory controls. Deleting a conversation doesn't necessarily delete an existing saved memory.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Transient uploads</td> <td>Eligible temporary Enterprise uploads outside Library can expire after 48 hours unless another applicable retention setting applies.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Connected-app content</td> <td>Source-system records follow that system's policies. Copies saved to a conversation, project, Library, or synced index follow the rules for their saved location.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Cloud browser data</td> <td>Hosted browser data is separate from local browser data. Users can remove saved cloud browser cookies through the applicable settings.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Compliance records</td> <td>Compliance Logs Platform records are available for 30 days. Exported copies follow the receiving system's retention policy.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Deleting a conversation, removing a Library file or saved memory, disconnecting an app, and clearing hosted browser data are separate actions. Review the relevant storage location instead of assuming one action removes every copy. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8983778-chat-and-file-retention-policies-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Chat and file retention policies (online)</a>.</p> <p>Retained conversation and execution context can help Work resume interrupted tasks and refer to earlier work. Consider that continuity alongside your security requirements when setting retention.</p> <p>Eligible Enterprise and Edu workspaces can use Enterprise Key Management for supported stored content, including supported hosted execution snapshots when customer-managed encryption is required. Coverage varies by data category and deployment. Rotating a key doesn't delete existing data or, by itself, deny access to earlier encrypted content. Revoking or disabling key access is a separate action that can disrupt supported workflows. Neither replaces a retention or deletion policy.</p> <p>Data residency and inference residency apply only to eligible content and supported workloads, subject to the organization's agreement, region, and configuration. Connected apps, external providers, and some processing or synced indexes can follow separate location rules. Verify support for the product, integration, and region. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9903489-data-residency-and-inference-residency-for-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Data residency and inference residency (online)</a>.</p> <p>OpenAI API <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Zero Data Retention</a> is an API-specific control and doesn't define retention for ChatGPT Work.</p> <h2 id=\"administrator-access-controls\">Administrator access controls</h2> <p>Enable <strong>Allow local computer access</strong> under Work Cloud. <strong>Use Codex locally on the ChatGPT desktop app</strong> is not a prerequisite. If <code>enforce_residency</code> is enabled in any cloud policy, <strong>Allow local computer access</strong> is disabled for both Work and dots. This safeguard does not configure workspace residency or, by itself, disable Work Cloud or dots. Before enabling it, review or create the global cloud baseline in <strong>Agent Security</strong>.</p> <p>For policy API, migration, and Terraform guidance, see <a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad?anchor=what-carries-over\">What carries over</a>.</p> <p>Review each control in the context where it applies:</p> <ul> <li> <p><strong>Enterprise requirements.</strong> For Work with local access and dots, supported Global policy applies through the shared cloud orchestrator when managed policy is enabled. Applicable local <code>requirements.toml</code> requirements govern execution on a connected computer. Work cloud containers and dots cloud computers use their own execution configuration and requirements, rather than the managed environment bundle used by other executor types. Local execution restrictions do not automatically apply to these cloud computers. Review cloud capability permissions and test local and cloud execution separately.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Local execution.</strong> Supported device controls still apply to steps that run on the connected computer.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Cloud execution policy.</strong> Work Cloud manages its own execution environment under existing Work Cloud policies. The local environment's managed execution policy does not carry over. Desktop browser site rules do not become cloud-browser restrictions.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Keep orchestrator controls, including approvals and web search, in Global. Use the dedicated Allowed approval policies and Allowed web search modes controls where available, and TOML for other supported fields. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">Configuration Reference</a> for the field list and execution scope.</p> <p>Turning off Local computer access with Work Cloud interrupts currently running turns. Users can start a new turn in an existing cloud conversation. That turn automatically uses Work Cloud without access to local files.</p> <p>Review the controls that apply to each part of a cloud task:</p> <ul> <li> <p><strong>Work Cloud and Work Local:</strong> Where independent controls are available, manage cloud and local Work as distinct controls in <strong>Admin Console</strong> &gt; <strong>Permissions</strong>. In other workspaces, local Work can share a control with Codex Local.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Apps and plugins:</strong> Choose which integrations are available and which people or roles can use them.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Connected-account actions:</strong> Review account permissions, application scopes, and available action or confirmation controls.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Browser and networking:</strong> Assess cloud browser access and code or shell public-network access independently.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Enable <strong>Work Cloud</strong> only for approved users or groups. For cloud-only Work without cross-device sync, enable Work Cloud and disable Work Local for the intended role, where separate controls are available. Cross-device sync requires both permissions. Turning either permission off and saving the change also turns off Sync. Where local Work and Codex share a control, review the effect on both before disabling local execution. These controls don't prevent an authorized person from intentionally uploading a file to a cloud task.</p> <p>For supported role permissions with <strong>Default</strong>, <strong>On</strong>, and <strong>Off</strong> states, <strong>Default</strong> inherits the workspace setting, <strong>On</strong> grants access through that role, and <strong>Off</strong> does not grant access through that role. Ordinary role permissions combine additively, so another assigned role can still grant access. Lockdown Mode and product eligibility apply separately. Some Work and plugin settings use different, two-state controls. Verify effective access across all assigned roles. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11750701-rbac\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Role-based access control (online)</a>.</p> <p>Where available, the <strong>Work Cloud</strong> permission applies across supported web, mobile, and desktop experiences. It doesn't independently select which of those surfaces can run cloud tasks. Consider device-management or other access controls if a deployment must exclude a particular surface.</p> <h2 id=\"audit-and-compliance-visibility\">Audit and compliance visibility</h2> <p>For eligible Enterprise and Edu workspaces, the Compliance Logs Platform can include supported Work prompts and responses. Connected-app calls have separate logs, and available source-system audit records vary by integration. Supported compliance endpoints can provide access to eligible Library files.</p> <p>Coverage depends on the event and the system where it occurs. Don't assume every shell command, browser interaction, app invocation, file operation, or approval appears in a customer-visible compliance export.</p> <p>Endpoint monitoring can observe the ChatGPT client or network traffic on managed devices, but can't inspect actions inside the hosted execution environment. Use supported Work, compliance, and connected-system records instead.</p> <p>Review current compliance event coverage alongside workspace reporting, connected-system audit logs, and the retention policies of systems receiving exported records. See the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9261474-compliance-api-for-chatgpt-enterprise-edu-and-chatgpt-for-teachers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Compliance Platform (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"verify-cloud-access-and-controls\">Verify cloud access and controls</h2> <p>Test cloud access with a task that reflects your team’s work. For example, a security team could compare an approved vendor advisory with an authorized inventory and review a draft exposure assessment before deciding what to do. If cloud browsing or connected apps are unavailable, provide the advisory and an approved inventory extract directly.</p> <p>Enable only the access the task requires. Check connected-account permissions, retention settings, and available audit records. Tell users which results and actions require human review. For rollout planning, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">Admin rollout guide</a>.</p>"};
